sodium.options.actinium.production_diagnostics.name=Production Diagnostics
sodium.options.actinium.production_diagnostics.tooltip=Logs Demonica environment, configuration, and key mixin application facts. Useful for comparing development and production behavior.
sodium.options.actinium.gl_debug.name=GL State Debug
sodium.options.actinium.gl_debug.tooltip=Logs detailed Iris and GLSM state checkpoints while a shader pack is active. This can be very noisy.
sodium.options.actinium.lwjgl_debug.name=LWJGL Debug Context
sodium.options.actinium.lwjgl_debug.tooltip=Requests an OpenGL debug context and installs the KHR_debug driver callback, logging the driver's own error messages with stack traces. Requires restarting the game to take effect.
sodium.options.actinium.pbr_debug.name=PBR Texture Debug
sodium.options.actinium.pbr_debug.tooltip=Logs PBR texture discovery, atlas animation, and lifecycle diagnostics, and exports loaded PBR atlases for inspection. This can be noisy and use additional disk space.
sodium.options.actinium.cloud_control_debug.name=Cloud Control Debug
sodium.options.actinium.cloud_control_debug.tooltip=Logs the specific colortex4 and colortex14 control pixels that Bliss cloud passes read. Use this to diagnose missing volumetric clouds.
sodium.options.actinium.perf_debug.name=Render Timing Debug
sodium.options.actinium.perf_debug.tooltip=Logs CPU timing windows for Demonica render pipeline checkpoints and shader transform cache hits, misses, and timings.
sodium.options.actinium.gpu_perf_debug.name=GPU Timing Debug
sodium.options.actinium.gpu_perf_debug.tooltip=Adds GPU timer queries to render timing debug. Use only while diagnosing production issues.
sodium.options.actinium.frame_gl_error_check.name=Pre-Render GL Error Check
sodium.options.actinium.frame_gl_error_check.tooltip=Keeps Minecraft's pre-render GL error checkpoint enabled and logs the checkpoint stage.
sodium.options.actinium.post_render_gl_error_check.name=Post-Render GL Error Check
sodium.options.actinium.post_render_gl_error_check.tooltip=Keeps Minecraft's post-render GL error checkpoint enabled and logs the checkpoint stage.
sodium.options.actinium.redirector_debug.name=Redirector Class Debug
sodium.options.actinium.redirector_debug.tooltip=Logs which classes the early and late Demonica redirectors transform during startup. Requires restarting the game to take effect.
sodium.options.actinium.redirector_log_spam.name=Redirector Method Logspam
sodium.options.actinium.redirector_log_spam.tooltip=Logs each redirected GL or GlStateManager method call while classes are being transformed. Very noisy. Requires restarting the game to take effect.
sodium.options.actinium.redirector_class_dump.name=Redirector Class Dump
sodium.options.actinium.redirector_class_dump.tooltip=Dumps PRE and POST transformed classes into the ASM_GTNH folder under the game directory. Useful for verifying production redirects. Requires restarting the game to take effect.
sodium.options.actinium.model_renderer_batching.name=Model Renderer Batching
sodium.options.actinium.model_renderer_batching.tooltip=Submits entity model part quads through Demonica's batched model path instead of vanilla's per-box renderer. Disable this first if player models or armor turn partially transparent under shader packs. Turning it off is closer to the upstream Angelica/vanilla path.
sodium.options.actinium.ignore_framebuffer_errors.name=Ignore Framebuffer Errors
sodium.options.actinium.ignore_framebuffer_errors.tooltip=Allows framebuffers that fail the graphics driver's completeness check to be used anyway. If you are running on an Android device (e.g. the MobileGlues renderer) and some rendering does not work correctly, try enabling this. Warning: reduces the diagnosability of real graphics errors.
options.actinium.shaderPackSelection=Iris Shader Packs
options.actinium.loadingScreenFramerateLimit=Loading Screen FPS Limit
options.actinium.loadingScreenFramerateLimit.tooltip=Limits frames per second while no world is loaded, including the loading screen. Defaults to 60.
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.name=Biome Color Noise
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.tooltip=Adds subtle position-based variation to grass, foliage, and water colors within the same biome (Ambient Environment style). Tint colors are baked into chunk meshes, so chunks need to be rebuilt (or the world re-entered) for changes to take effect.
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.grass.name=Biome Noise: Grass
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.grass.tooltip=Intensity of the position-based color noise applied to grass tints, in percent. Higher values make the mottling more visible.
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.foliage.name=Biome Noise: Foliage
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.foliage.tooltip=Intensity of the position-based color noise applied to foliage tints, in percent. Higher values make the mottling more visible.
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.water.name=Biome Noise: Water
sodium.options.actinium.biome_color_noise.water.tooltip=Intensity of the position-based color noise applied to water tints, in percent. Higher values make the mottling more visible.
celeritas.options.fast_block_renderer.name=Use Fast Block Renderer
celeritas.options.fast_block_renderer.tooltip=Enables the backported faster block renderer from newer Celeritas versions, which has better performance but may look slightly different.
sodium.options.pages.debug=Debug
celeritas.options.fullscreen_mode.name=Fullscreen Mode
celeritas.options.fullscreen_mode.tooltip=Controls how the game enters fullscreen. Borderless uses a monitor-sized undecorated window instead of exclusive fullscreen.
celeritas.options.fullscreen_mode.off=Off
celeritas.options.fullscreen_mode.exclusive=Exclusive Fullscreen
celeritas.options.fullscreen_mode.borderless=Borderless
sodium.options.streaming_upload_strategy.name=Streaming Upload Strategy
sodium.options.streaming_upload_strategy.tooltip=Controls how GLSM uploads immediate Tessellator draw data to the GPU. Map Buffer Range matches GTNH Angelica's default and is usually the fastest option; Buffer Data is the most conservative fallback.
sodium.options.streaming_upload_strategy.buffer_data=Buffer Data
sodium.options.streaming_upload_strategy.buffer_sub_data=Buffer Sub Data
sodium.options.streaming_upload_strategy.map_buffer_range=Map Buffer Range
sodium.options.model_renderer_display_lists.name=Model Renderer Display Lists
sodium.options.model_renderer_display_lists.tooltip=Compiles static entity model part geometry into GLSM display-list VBOs and reuses it across frames. This reduces CPU overhead from many small model draws. Disable this if entity models render incorrectly.
sodium.options.fast_lit_item_rendering.name=Fast Lit Item Rendering
sodium.options.fast_lit_item_rendering.tooltip=Skips Forge's per-segment lit item renderer for item models that do not use custom lightmap or diffuse-lighting state. This reduces CPU overhead for common item models while preserving Forge's path for emissive or special-lit items.
sodium.options.fast_lit_item_display_lists.name=Fast Lit Item Display Lists
sodium.options.fast_lit_item_display_lists.tooltip=Caches stable untinted baked item models in GLSM display lists after the fast lit item path accepts them. Disable this if some item models render stale or incorrectly.
sodium.options.allow_direct_memory_access.name=Allow Direct Memory Access
sodium.options.allow_direct_memory_access.tooltip=If enabled, some critical code paths will be allowed to use direct memory access for performance. This often greatly reduces CPU overhead for chunk and entity rendering, but can make it harder to diagnose some bugs and crashes. You should only disable this if you've been asked to or otherwise know what you're doing.
sodium.options.dynamic_fov.name=Dynamic FOV
sodium.options.dynamic_fov.tooltip=If disabled, the field of view stays at the configured value instead of widening while sprinting or flying and narrowing while drawing a bow.\n\nThis only affects the dynamic factor: the underwater and death-camera scaling still apply.
